  "worked_solution": "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}\u2061x={sec}^{2}\u2061x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}\u2061x={sec}^{2}\u2061x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}\u2061x-{tan}^{2}\u2061x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}\u2061x-2{sec}^{2}\u2061x+1+{tan}^{2}\u2061x={sec}^{4}\u2061x-2{sec}^{2}\u2061x+1+{sec}^{2}\u2061x-1\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression and use again $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{4}\u2061x-2{sec}^{2}\u2061x+1+{sec}^{2}\u2061x-1 & ={sec}^{4}\u2061x-2{sec}^{2}\u2061x+\\cancel{1}+{sec}^{2}\u2061x-\\cancel{1} \\\\  & ={sec}^{4}\u2061x-{sec}^{2}\u2061x \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}\u2061x\\cdot ({sec}^{2}\u2061x-1) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}\u2061x\\cdot {tan}^{2}\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}\u2061x-2{sec}^{2}\u2061x+1+{tan}^{2}\u2061x={sec}^{2}\u2061x{tan}^{2}\u2061x.\n$$",
